['|Case|:functionality_1_user_registration\n```\nCLASS NewsReader:\n    FUNCTION register_user(username, password)\n        OPEN users.txt IN APPEND MODE\n        WRITE username|password TO FILE\n        RETURN True\n\nROUTE /register (GET/POST):\n    IF METHOD IS POST:\n        GET username FROM form\n        GET password FROM form\n        CALL news_reader.register_user(username, password)\n        REDIRECT TO /login\n    ELSE:\n        RENDER register.html TEMPLATE\n```\n```\nCLASS AuthManager:\n    FUNCTION register(username, password):\n        TRY:\n            OPEN users.txt IN append+read mode\n            FOR each line in file:\n                IF username exists:\n                    RETURN False (duplicate user)\n            WRITE username:password to file\n            RETURN True\n        EXCEPT IOError:\n            RETURN False\n\nROUTE /register (GET/POST):\n    IF POST request:\n        GET username, password from form\n        IF AuthManager.register(username, password) SUCCESS:\n            REDIRECT to login\n        ELSE:\n            RENDER registration.html WITH error="Username exists"\n    ELSE:\n        RENDER registration.html\n```\n```\nCLASS UserAuth:\n    METHOD __init__(users_file=\'users.txt\'):\n        IF users.txt NOT EXISTS:\n            CREATE users.txt\n    METHOD register(username, password):\n        OPEN users.txt IN READ+APPEND MODE\n        FOR EACH LINE IN users.txt:\n            IF username EXISTS:\n                RETURN False (duplicate)\n        WRITE username|password TO users.txt\n        RETURN True\n\nROUTE /register (GET/POST):\n    IF POST REQUEST:\n        username = FORM[\'username\']\n        password = FORM[\'password\']\n        IF UserAuth.register(username, password) SUCCESS:\n            FLASH "Registration successful"\n            REDIRECT TO /login\n        ELSE:\n            FLASH "Username exists"\n    RENDER register.html\n```\n\nThird-party Libraries:\n- Flask: Handles HTTP routing and request processing\n- werkzeug: Security utilities\n- os: Checks file existence\n\n2. |Case|:functionality_2_user_login\n```\nCLASS NewsReader:\n    FUNCTION authenticate(username, password)\n        OPEN users.txt IN READ MODE\n        FOR EACH LINE IN FILE:\n            SPLIT line INTO stored_user, stored_pass\n            IF stored_user == username AND stored_pass == password:\n                RETURN True\n        RETURN False\n\nROUTE /login (GET/POST):\n    IF METHOD IS POST:\n        GET username FROM form\n        GET password FROM form\n        IF news_reader.authenticate(username, password):\n            SET session[\'username\'] = username\n            REDIRECT TO /dashboard\n        ELSE:\n            RENDER login.html WITH error message\n    ELSE:\n        RENDER login.html\n```\n```\nCLASS AuthManager:\n    FUNCTION login(username, password):\n        TRY:\n            OPEN users.txt IN read mode\n            FOR each line in file:\n                IF stored_username == username AND stored_password == password:\n                    RETURN True\n            RETURN False\n        EXCEPT IOError:\n            RETURN False\n\nROUTE /login (GET/POST):\n    IF POST request:\n        GET username, password from form\n        IF AuthManager.login(username, password) SUCCESS:\n            SET session[\'username\'] = username\n            REDIRECT to dashboard\n        ELSE:\n            RENDER login.html WITH error="Invalid credentials"\n    ELSE:\n        RENDER login.html\n```\n```\nMETHOD login(username, password):\n    OPEN users.txt IN READ MODE\n    FOR EACH LINE IN users.txt:\n        IF username AND password MATCH:\n            RETURN True\n    RETURN False\n\nROUTE /login (GET/POST):\n    IF POST REQUEST:\n        username = FORM[\'username\']\n        password = FORM[\'password\']\n        IF UserAuth.login(username, password):\n            SET SESSION[\'username\'] = username\n            REDIRECT TO /dashboard\n        ELSE:\n            FLASH "Invalid credentials"\n    RENDER login.html\n```\n\nThird-party Libraries:\n- Flask.session: Manages user sessions\n\n3. ', "|Case|:functionality_3_browse_news_categories\n```\nCLASS NewsReader:\n    FUNCTION get_categories()\n        categories = []\n        OPEN categories.txt IN READ MODE\n        FOR EACH LINE IN FILE:\n            APPEND line.strip() TO categories\n        RETURN categories\n\n    FUNCTION get_news(category=None)\n        news_items = []\n        OPEN news.txt IN READ MODE\n        FOR EACH LINE IN FILE:\n            SPLIT line INTO parts\n            IF category IS None OR parts[4] == category:\n                APPEND news_item TO news_items\n        RETURN news_items\n\nROUTE /dashboard:\n    IF 'username' NOT IN session:\n        REDIRECT TO /login\n    GET category FROM request.args\n    IF category EXISTS:\n        CALL news_reader.get_news(category)\n    ELSE:\n        CALL news_reader.get_news()\n    GET categories FROM news_reader.get_categories()\n    RENDER dashboard.html WITH username, news_items, categories\n```\n```\nCLASS NewsFeed:\n    FUNCTION _load_articles():\n        OPEN articles.txt\n        PARSE each line as JSON\n        RETURN list of articles\n\n    FUNCTION get_categories():\n        articles = _load_articles()\n        EXTRACT unique categories from articles\n        RETURN list of categories\n\nROUTE /dashboard:\n    IF user NOT logged in: REDIRECT to login\n    GET query, category from request\n    IF query:\n        articles = NewsFeed.search_articles(query)\n    ELSE IF category:\n        articles = FILTER articles WHERE category matches\n    ELSE:\n        articles = NewsFeed._load_articles()\n    RENDER dashboard.html WITH articles, categories\n```\n```\nMETHOD get_articles(category=None):\n    OPEN articles.txt IN READ MODE\n    FOR EACH LINE IN articles.txt:\n        PARSE article_data (id, title, summary, content, category, source)\n        IF category IS None OR article.category == category:\n            APPEND article TO results\n    RETURN results\n\nROUTE /dashboard:\n    IF 'username' NOT IN SESSION:\n        REDIRECT TO /login\n    category = REQUEST.args.get('category')\n    articles = NewsFeed.get_articles(category)\n    RENDER dashboard.html WITH articles, categories\n```\n\nThird-party Libraries:\n- Flask.request: Handles URL query parameters\n\n4. |Case|:functionality_4_search_news\n```\nCLASS NewsReader:\n    FUNCTION search_news(query)\n        results = []\n        OPEN news.txt IN READ MODE\n        FOR EACH LINE IN FILE:\n            SPLIT line INTO parts\n            IF query IN parts[1] OR query IN parts[2]:\n                APPEND news_item TO results\n        RETURN results\n\nROUTE /dashboard:\n    IF 'username' NOT IN session:\n        REDIRECT TO /login\n    GET query FROM request.args\n    IF query EXISTS:\n        CALL news_reader.search_news(query)\n    ELSE:\n        CALL news_reader.get_news()\n    RENDER dashboard.html WITH search results\n```\n```\nCLASS NewsFeed:\n    FUNCTION search_articles(query):\n        articles = _load_articles()\n        RETURN articles WHERE query matches title/summary/content (case-insensitive)\n\nROUTE /dashboard:\n    IF query provided:\n        articles = NewsFeed.search_articles(query)\n    RENDER dashboard.html WITH articles\n```\n```\nMETHOD search_articles(query):\n    OPEN articles.txt IN READ MODE\n    FOR EACH LINE IN articles.txt:\n        PARSE article_data (id, title, summary, content, category, source)\n        IF query IN title OR query IN summary (case-insensitive):\n            APPEND article TO results\n    RETURN results\n\nROUTE /dashboard:\n    query = REQUEST.args.get('query')\n    IF query:\n        articles = NewsFeed.search_articles(query)\n    ELSE:\n        articles = NewsFeed.get_articles()\n    RENDER dashboard.html WITH articles, categories\n```\n\n5. ", '|Case|:functionality_5_view_article_summaries\n```\nCLASS NewsReader:\n    FUNCTION get_article(article_id)\n        OPEN news.txt IN READ MODE\n        FOR EACH LINE IN FILE:\n            SPLIT line INTO parts\n            IF parts[0] == article_id:\n                RETURN article_details\n        RETURN None\n\nROUTE /article/<article_id>:\n    IF \'username\' NOT IN session:\n        REDIRECT TO /login\n    CALL news_reader.get_article(article_id)\n    IF article EXISTS:\n        RENDER article.html WITH article\n    ELSE:\n        REDIRECT TO /dashboard\n```\n```\nCLASS NewsFeed:\n    FUNCTION get_article_details(article_id):\n        articles = _load_articles()\n        RETURN article WHERE id matches\n\nROUTE /article/<article_id>:\n    IF user NOT logged in: REDIRECT to login\n    article = NewsFeed.get_article_details(article_id)\n    IF article exists:\n        RENDER article.html WITH article\n    ELSE:\n        REDIRECT to dashboard\n```\n```\nMETHOD get_article(article_id):\n    OPEN articles.txt IN READ MODE\n    FOR EACH LINE IN articles.txt:\n        PARSE article_data (id, title, summary, content, category, source)\n        IF id == article_id:\n            RETURN article\n    RETURN None\n\nROUTE /article/<article_id>:\n    IF \'username\' NOT IN SESSION:\n        REDIRECT TO /login\n    article = NewsFeed.get_article(article_id)\n    IF article NOT FOUND:\n        FLASH "Article not found"\n        REDIRECT TO /dashboard\n    RENDER article.html WITH article\n```\n\n6. |Case|:functionality_6_user_logout\n```\nROUTE /logout:\n    REMOVE \'username\' FROM session\n    REDIRECT TO /login\n```\n```\nROUTE /logout:\n    REMOVE \'username\' from session\n    REDIRECT to login\n```\n```\nROUTE /logout:\n    REMOVE \'username\' FROM SESSION\n    REDIRECT TO /login\n```']
